atlas external

architecture external-world-closure-product
  canonical_name ExternalWorldClosureProduct
  family surface
  domain Surface / Public World
  layer surface/public
  semantic_question How does one addressed public World become a coherent human product and a machine resource without assembling two different candidate sets?
  purpose Compiles a bounded, content-addressed public World closure from the measured ExternalEstate reservoir. A product-map closure names every World and grammar aperture, then each declared World and its participating interaction grammars become human and machine product routes through the same compiler, so a reader and machine inspect the same candidates, lenses and limits.
  maturity measured
  consumes ExternalEstateDensity
  consumes SurfaceDemand
  publishes PublicWorldClosure
  publishes PublicWorldCatalogue
  publishes HumanWorldProjection
  publishes MachineWorldProjection
  node_types PublicWorldClosure
  node_types PublicWorldCatalogue
  node_types SurfaceLens
  edge_types lowers
  edge_types projects
  invariant the HTML and JSON carriers expose the same closure digest and candidate identities; a carrier may differ in representation but never in World membership
  invariant a public World lens is a bounded deterministic presentation ranking over observed candidates, not an ActorClosure, provider admission, evidence admission, institutional fact, right, payment, settlement or effect
  invariant a public World closure carries the same content-addressed formation-candidate projection to human and machine carriers: possible publication, decision service, coordination, market, place-service and small-institution artifacts expose counted observed signal coverage and missing signals, never an automatic launch or authority claim
  invariant the public formation-catalogue carrier enumerates every declared World through the same bounded formation compiler and has no semantic ranking, priority, need, demand or launch implication
  invariant World aliases are explicit composition declarations and retain the requested and resolved names in the closure
  invariant a focused grammar lens is a smaller addressed closure with its own digest; it is not an HTML-only tab or a route-specific application
  invariant a visible public lens lowers only the selected presentation cell's declared renderers and visible sections; presentation changes the carrier grammar but never candidate membership, owner standing or authority
  invariant the product map names declared World and grammar apertures without claiming each candidate is admitted or actionable; focused closures retain that candidate boundary
  invariant conditional requests may reuse a public closure only while its exact closure digest matches; a changed corpus-derived closure receives a new validator
  invariant a reconnecting public World runtime asks this owner for the complete, content-addressed Scene at its declared scene carrier; 304 preserves the exact Scene it already holds, while a changed digest supplies a successor Scene and never a client-compiled candidate patch
  invariant a changed published corpus stamp clears only the disposable public candidate/lens indexes before recompilation; it does not mutate ForeignTwin, evidence, provider, authority or effect owner state
  invariant when a deployment binds the native AddressPlane index, the public closure emits only candidates returned by that index's World-mask witness as eligible-for-further-consideration and fails closed if configured to require the witness
  invariant a public source card may initiate only an explicit no-body transport check; that receipt cannot establish provider standing, evidence, authority, payment, settlement or effect
  forbidden_inference a public World closure -> private or institutional World state
  forbidden_inference a candidate lens -> exact-owner selection or lawful data combination
  forbidden_inference a cached public closure -> continued source availability or effect authority
  forbidden_inference a public Scene reconciliation -> an ActorClosure, a queued external effect, a provider admission or a right to apply a partial owner result
  forbidden_inference a rendered /external-estate World page -> the human product page; it is a corpus and debugging carrier over candidates, and people read a subject through PageComposition at /w/<slug>, which composes admitted owner material into existing interaction languages rather than candidate cards
  source_path Aurekai/src/external-estate-runtime.mjs
  source_path Aurekai/src/external-estate-server.mjs
  source_path Aurekai/src/presentation-cell-catalog.mjs
  source_path Aurekai/tests/external-estate-runtime.test.mjs
  source_path Aurekai/tests/external-estate-server.test.mjs
  source_path Aurekai/docs/EXTERNAL_ESTATE_RUNTIME.md
  source_path deploy/systemd/external-estate.env.example
  witness Aurekai/tests/external-estate-runtime.test.mjs proves Farm Cold Chain Household compiles a real 131-occurrence public World closure with bounded lenses, and embeds the exact machine closure digest in the human projection
  witness Aurekai/tests/external-estate-server.test.mjs boots the public HTTP carrier, verifies HTML and JSON expose one closure digest, and proves an If-None-Match re-read returns 304 without a body
  witness Aurekai/tests/external-estate-server.test.mjs proves the HTTP formation-catalogue carrier returns the measured 30-World full-estate census with an exact closure digest
  witness Aurekai/tests/external-estate-runtime.test.mjs proves all 30 measured Worlds expose all 15 participating compiled grammar families as 450 focused product closures, and separately verifies every grammar can lower as a focused World lens
  witness Aurekai/tests/external-estate-server.test.mjs proves the server-rendered product map and its JSON carrier share one digest over 30 Worlds and 450 declared focused apertures
  witness Aurekai/tests/external-estate-runtime.test.mjs proves a rebuilt temporary corpus is re-read through the same public runtime without a process restart and invalidates only its disposable candidate indexes
  witness Aurekai/tests/external-estate-runtime.test.mjs proves the local 4,891-occurrence native AddressPlane index rejects 4,760 records before exact ownership for Farm Cold Chain Household and that all 131 survivors remain within the measured World reservoir
  witness Aurekai/tests/external-estate-runtime.test.mjs proves every rendered public World card exposes an explicit POST transport-check carrier and that the resulting human receipt names its no-body/non-admission boundary
  witness local 2026-09-15 server witness at 127.0.0.1:8872 returned Farm Cold Chain Household HTML and JSON with closure sha256:2bfb77eb17f049b210a63ec6d9a5d36712c3149eec2f6a8579d06ae91101576a, 131 occurrences and six eight-candidate lenses; an If-None-Match request returned 304 without a body
  source_lineage public product closure over the measured external estate

interaction external-world-closure-serves-human-and-machine
  source external-estate-density
  destination external-world-closure-product
  relation bounded_public_product_projection
  preserves requested/resolved World coordinate, observed candidate identity, deterministic lens selection, public candidate limits and closure digest
  drops ActorClosure, audience, institutional role, InformationPolicy decision, provider admission, evidence admission, financial authority, payment, settlement and effect authority
  forbidden_inference human World page or machine World resource -> provider readiness, admitted evidence, authority, payment, settlement or effect
  invalidates_on external corpus digest, World alias declaration, SurfaceDemand profile or public World closure compiler changes
  witness Aurekai/tests/external-estate-runtime.test.mjs
  witness Aurekai/tests/external-estate-server.test.mjs
  binding Aurekai/src/external-estate-runtime.mjs
  binding Aurekai/src/external-estate-server.mjs

interaction external-world-scene-reconciles-at-surface-runtime
  source external-world-closure-product
  destination surface-ir
  relation content_addressed_scene_reconciliation
  preserves exact prior closure digest, complete successor Scene, public actor scope, declared lenses, owner query plan and the candidate boundary
  drops ActorClosure, audience entitlement, authority, provider/evidence admission, payment, settlement, commitment and effect state
  forbidden_inference an owner Scene carrier -> permission for the browser to derive, replay or partially apply a changed candidate result
  invalidates_on external corpus digest, World alias declaration, SurfaceDemand profile, public World Scene compiler or SurfaceRuntime delta contract changes
  witness Aurekai/tests/external-estate-server.test.mjs
  witness cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/tests/surface_runtime_test.mjs
  binding Aurekai/src/external-estate-runtime.mjs
  binding Aurekai/src/external-estate-server.mjs
  binding cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/surface-runtime.mjs
